"""
Live changes for library administration. Subscriptions run only over the graphql-transport-ws
WebSocket on /graphql; queries and mutations run only over HTTP POST on /graphql.

A subscription delivers changes from the moment it registers. It sends no snapshot and replays
nothing missed. To build current state, subscribe first, then query
`libraries { id name status scanStartedOn scanCompletedOn }`, and apply each later change by
library id.

Each field delivers one library's changes in the order they were committed. There is no order
across libraries or across fields: `libraryAdded` and `libraryStatusChanged` for one library may
arrive in either order. `libraryStatusChanged` delivers the library as the server reads it after
the change, so a client may miss an intermediate status, but the last change it receives carries
the latest status. A subscription never completes normally while the server runs.

A field error does not end the operation. When a selected field of one change fails to resolve,
the server delivers that change as null with errors, and later changes still arrive. A client
skips the null change and may query `libraries` again to recover the state it missed.

These errors end the operation:
FORBIDDEN when the caller is not a ServerAdmin,
AUTHORIZATION_UNAVAILABLE when authorization cannot be decided,
SUBSCRIPTION_OVERFLOW when changes arrived faster than the server could resolve them,
TOO_MANY_OPERATIONS when the connection already runs its maximum number of operations.
After SUBSCRIPTION_OVERFLOW, subscribe again and query `libraries` again.
"""
type Subscription {
    """
    A library's status or scan times changed. Delivers the library after each change, or null with
    errors when a selected field fails to resolve. ServerAdmin only.
    """
    libraryStatusChanged: Library

    """
    A library was added. Delivers the new library, or null with errors when a selected field fails
    to resolve. ServerAdmin only.
    """
    libraryAdded: Library

    """
    A library was removed. Delivers the removed library's id, or null with errors when a selected
    field fails to resolve. ServerAdmin only.
    """
    libraryRemoved: LibraryRemoval
}
